<title>FRANCE: French court says BA statement &quot;excessive&quot;.</title>
<headline>French court says BA statement &quot;excessive&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>A French commercial court said that a statement by British Airways that the court had accepted the British airline's rescue bid for ailing French carrier Air Liberte was &quot;excessive&quot;.</p>
<p>&quot;The statement by British Airways is totally excessive. It is an interpretation. In a legal sense, there is nothing in the way to stop any other bid than theirs,&quot; court president Dominique Leveque told Reuters by telephone.</p>
</text>
